Unreleased

 Fixes:
    - A source document with unreadable frontmatter (for example an unquoted value containing ": ") no longer vanishes silently:
      it is recorded in BuildPlan.invalid_docs and counted as invalid=N in the build summary; the log gives the YAML line, column and problem
    - apphelp: with strict on, an invalid document fails the build as DOC_INVALID, together with the other metadata problems
    - New repo.json switch fail_on_invalid (default false) makes any theme fail the build on invalid documents
    - kb4it verify exits 1 when it finds a non-conformant file or a theme problem, so it can gate CI

2026-10-01 Tomás Vírseda <tomasvirseda@gmail.com>

 * Released version 0.7.9

 Features:
    - New theme: apphelp (help sites for applications; strict metadata, offline search, help ids, go.html)
    - C1: Markdown links to .md files are rewritten to .html; unknown targets log LINK_BROKEN
    - C2: source and target are relative to the repository root (PATH_CWD_RELATIVE fallback); create writes them
    - C3: the backend no longer writes into source/; Builder.create_page_about_app()
    - C4: Date is optional; undated documents come after dated ones and show an empty date cell
    - C6: theme.json metadata_pages turns the metadata pages off
    - C7: theme.json deploy_dirs deploys only the listed theme folders
    - C8: repo.json publish_sources controls copying the sources to the target
    - C9: optional logic/verify.py theme hook
    - C10: Builder.site_signature()
    - YAML null frontmatter values become []
    - Tests run with ./scripts/devel/test.sh; CI runs them and checks the wheel for every tracked theme

 Custom themes:
    - The about pages are no longer added for every theme. A custom theme must call
      create_page_about_kb4it() and create_page_about_app() in its build() to get them.
      An untouched generated source/about_kb4it.md from older versions is removed.


